- 5.1.1       New address test. Every socket now gets a "march" across all of its rows and
              all of its columns, replacing the old check that only tried one address line at
              a time. The old one could not see two rows (or two columns) landing on the same
              cells inside the chip, and neither could the pattern tests -- widest on the
              411000. Costs ~45 ms on a 4164 and ~130 ms on a 411000, and the shared routine
              freed 184 bytes by replacing five separate address tests.
