                18-pin always did; 16-pin and 20-pin ran it once before the loop. Loop mode
                is the warm/soak test, so the march belongs inside it -- a decoder that
                only aliases once the part has been busy, or a cell that stops holding,
                is what that mode is for. Adds ~45-96 ms to an iteration of seconds.
