                undriven, and socket pin 13 was missing from the 18-pin map.
              Verified with a logic analyser, cycle-exact on thirteen parts across all
              four sockets: 4164, 4816, 41257, 3732-H, 4116, 4027, 4416, 4464, 411000 and
              all four 514xxx. Every march block hit its predicted edge count, and tRAS
              stayed inside spec everywhere -- 10 us on the NMOS types, ~100 us page mode.

=======================================================================================
 OPEN POINTS / KNOWN LIMITATIONS  (as of 5.1.1)
=======================================================================================
Not yet verified on hardware
 - TMS4532 (both halves) and MSM3732-L: no part available, only ever exercised through a
   4164 standing in for them. The MSM3732-H is verified on a real one.
 - 41256, 4164-2ms and the 2114 were not re-measured on 5.1.1. Each shares its code path
   with a type that was, so what is unverified is the geometry, not the logic. The 41256
   was measured on 5.1.0; the 4164-2ms is only reached when a 4164 fails its 4 ms pass.

Deliberately not covered
 - 41257 nibble read-back samples 31-94 ns after CAS-low, below tCAC. The extra NOP would
   cost 4 cycles inside a RAS window that already measures 10.00 us against a 10 us limit.
 - Coupling faults have no guarantee, only the checkerboard and two random passes. In
   particular the column order is never reversed, so a transition-coupling fault between
   two column neighbours is covered in one write direction only. Closing it means
   reversing eight burst loops and re-measuring eight chip types; a full March C- would
   cost 13 s on a 411000 and still not test retention.
 - Half-good parts whose quadrant pattern is ambiguous (a single quadrant) do not get
   their good half marched — there is no half to hold a safe coordinate in.
 - The VCC-short probe cannot cover PB4 (socket pin 11 / 13 / 15): it doubles as the
   display's SDA and something on that side holds the line up after the release. The
   ground check still covers those pins.

Build
 - Non-OLED build does not compile: printTestOK, drawQR, printQRandVersion and
   twoLineScreen are defined outside #ifdef OLED.
 - 104 bytes of flash free. The next feature needs room made first; the measured lever is
   checkAddressing_2114 (154 bytes), redundant because check_2114 is already a full
   March C- over the same address space.

